    <string name="about_what">Switches between the systems installed on this Galaxy Tab S9 Ultra by replacing the four boot partitions and restarting.</string>
    <string name="about_checks">Every image is checked by size before it is written, and the partition is read back afterwards. If anything does not match it stops, and nothing restarts.</string>
    <string name="about_untouched">Images are read from %1$s. Only boot, init_boot, vendor_boot and dtbo are written; vbmeta and super are never touched — the first would wipe Android’s data and the second is where its system lives.</string>
